nd delivers check while winning material — likely devastating.\n\nReason:  \n**N: e4-c3** delivers check to the White king (knight on c3 attacks a1), and the only way to respond is moving the king (Kd1 or Ke2), after which Black can follow up by capturing the now-loose pawn on d4 or increasing pressure. Additionally, this knight cannot be immediately dislodged, and White loses time defending. This move gains significant tempo and material advantage.\n\nAnswer: N: e4-c3"}
