bling faster development. Given that White may soon challenge the center or launch an attack, safeguarding the king is paramount. Additionally, after castling, Black can follow up with ...Nf6, ...Be7, etc., developing harmoniously.\n\nReason:  \nCastling maximizes long-term winning chances by securing the king, utilizing optimal piece coordination, and avoiding tactical vulnerabilities. It’s rare to find a safe opportunity to castle when the center is semi-open — here, the path is clear and not under direct threat. Other moves like Qd6 or Qh4 are tempting but risk misplacing the queen early if not supported.\n\nAnswer: K: e8-g8"}
